# Add Liquidity to Treble Swap
[Treble Swap](https://trebleswap.com/#ecosystem) is the first V4 DEX on Base; offering swaps, limit orders, perps, staking, and more. Rapidly listing dozens of Base-native projects, Treble is proving to be an excellent place for Internet Token to expand liquidity and intertwine itself deeper into the Base ecosystem.&#x20;

This proposal is to approve and transfer 1.5 ETH and 40,000,000 INT to the INT multi-sig wallet for the purpose of supplying liquidity to Treble in the form of an INT/USDC Liquidity Pool. The amount to be supplied is intentionally calculated so that liquidity in INT's Treble LP is proportionately sized in comparison to the main Uniswap LP, allowing trading volume on Treble to be competitive while also expanding buy-side and sell-side liquidity for INT equally.&#x20;

The goals for this collaboration include:

\- Expanded BASE ecosystem presence&#x20;
\- Additional Treasury income via trading fees
\- Additional utility for the INT token in the form of liquidity pooling and farming&#x20;
\- [Ecosystem collaboration opportunities with Treble and Treble-listed tokens  ](https://scratch-nation-1ab.notion.site/INT-Trebleswap-29b8091954f580a997dffeb45e442c8e)

# Update config of TicketAutomator
The TicketAutomator contract is used to help lottery players generate a bunch of tickets in a single transaction. It generates tickets by looping through ETH\<>INT swaps multiple times. Ticket generation (NFT minting) is quite gas-intensive and uses ~50k gas for a single ticket. Each loop (swap) consumes an additional ~250k gas. TicketAutomator is currently configured for 50 loops, and the ticket minter has its own configuration of 50 tickets per swap. Therefore theoretically 2,500 tickets can be generated within a single transaction, but this requires approximately 137M gas (50x250k + 2500x50k). Such a large-scale generation was possible before because the Base chain block gas limit is 150M.



However, the Base chain configuration changed on 17 September 2025 with the introduction of a 25M gas limit per transaction (rather than per block). Consequently, TicketAutomator sometimes has difficulty generating even 50–100 tickets because the gas estimations from some wallets are too high and exceed the chain limit.&#x20;

[https://docs.base.org/base-chain/network-information/block-building#per-transaction-gas-maximum](https://docs.base.org/base-chain/network-information/block-building#per-transaction-gas-maximum)&#x20;



This Tally vote alters the configuration of TicketAutomator by lowering the MaxLoops value from 50 to 20, leaving all the other configuration values unchanged. This should enable the contract to generate ~400 tickets per transaction within the current Base Chain gas limitations.

# Replace TradeFeeCallback contract
TradeFeeCallback contract is responsible for calculating the fees paid to the main INT\<>WETH swap pool and generating the corresponding number of tickets. Among other things the contract  checks whether an INT transfers are to/from an external Uniswap pool  in an attempt to disable third-party liquidity. This check alone reverts with some smart wallets (for example Base Smart Wallet) and prevents legitimate INT transfers.



**An updated TradeFeeCallback contract  without an external pools check has been deployed at address 0x9D9ee2708B18D8b28C3830a5145B6933BA47DE28. This Tally vote is intended to properly set up the configuration and roles.**



If necessary, external liquidity pools can still be blocked in the future with the help of the AllowListCallback contract, which was deployed a long time ago at address: 0xfd5BBCA6942AC19c6Ce7a65b11F3521237172079.



The on-chain actions attached to this vote can be separated into six different groups:



1\. Copy excluded fee accounts from old TradeFeeCallback contract (33 accounts in total);



2\. Set up Pool Ids and save pool state;



3\. Remove/Grant  DATA\_ADMIN and TICKET\_MINTER roles from old / to new TradeFeeCallback;



4\. Remove/Add Old/New contract callbacks to INT token config;



5\. Change config of RewardDistributorV2 contract to point to the new TradeFeeCallback;



6\.  Transfer 1 INT from/to the treasury to test whether transfers are still working.
